{"traceId":"f9f04bce717f013ccfe6acfcf4af970f","spanId":"7189cc96d7615265","name":"execute_tool search_documents","kind":1,"startTimeUnixNano":"1793951712423254143","endTimeUnixNano":"1793951712428022812","attributes":[{"key":"gen_ai.operation.name","value":{"stringValue":"execute_tool"}},{"key":"gen_ai.tool.name","value":{"stringValue":"search_documents"}},{"key":"gen_ai.tool.call.id","value":{"stringValue":"call_7e645f293afcd49a676ddd20"}},{"key":"evals.tool.arguments","value":{"stringValue":"{\"query\": \"income tax slabs new regime 2026-27\"}"}},{"key":"evals.tool.is_error","value":{"boolValue":false}},{"key":"evals.tool.result","value":{"stringValue":"{\"results\":[{\"doc_id\":\"kb-bulletin-2026-11\",\"title\":\"Kaveri Bank (fictional): rates and rules bulletin, November 2026\",\"date\":\"2026-11-06\",\"section\":\"Income tax: the Income-tax Act, 2025 and the tax year\",\"passage\":\"Income tax: the Income-tax Act, 2025 and the tax year\\nIncome for the year from 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027 is taxed under the Income-tax Act, 2025, which uses a \\\"tax year\\\" in place of the old \\\"previous year\\\" and \\\"assessment year\\\". The current tax year is 2026-27.\\n\\nSources: Ministry of Finance, \\\"Memorandum Explaining the Provisions in the Finance Bill, 2026\\\", Part II, \\\"Rates of income-tax in respect of income liable to tax for the tax year 2026-27 for the purposes of Income-tax Act, 2025\\\", https://indiabudget.gov.in/doc/memo.pdf; Income Tax Department, \\\"Objective and scope of the New Act\\\", https://www.incometax.gov.in/iec/foportal/help/all-topics/e-filing-services/objective-and-scope-new-act (both checked 6 November 2026).\"},{\"doc_id\":\"kb-bulletin-2026-11\",\"title\":\"Kaveri Bank (fictional): rates and rules bulletin, November 2026\",\"date\":\"2026-11-06\",\"section\":\"Income tax slabs for individuals, new (default) regime, tax year 2026-27\",\"passage\":\"Income tax slabs for individuals, new (default) regime, tax year 2026-27\\nThe rates in section 202 of the Income-tax Act, 2025, on total income. Each rate applies only to the part of the income that falls in its band.\\n\\n| Total income | Rate of tax |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Up to ₹4,00,000 | Nil |\\n| ₹4,00,001 to ₹8,00,000 | 5% |\\n| ₹8,00,001 to ₹12,00,000 | 10% |\\n| ₹12,00,001 to ₹16,00,000 | 15% |\\n| ₹16,00,001 to ₹20,00,000 | 20% |\\n| ₹20,00,001 to ₹24,00,000 | 25% |\\n| Above ₹24,00,000 | 30% |\\n\\nThese are the default rates; a taxpayer may opt out of them under section 202(4). The Finance Bill, 2026 proposed no change to them.\\n\\nSource: Ministry of Finance, \\\"Memorandum Explaining the Provisions in the Finance Bill, 2026\\\", Part II, \\\"Tax rates under section 202\\\", https://indiabudget.gov.in/doc/memo.pdf (checked 6 November 2026).\"},{\"doc_id\":\"kb-bulletin-2026-11\",\"title\":\"Kaveri Bank (fictional): rates and rules bulletin, November 2026\",\"date\":\"2026-11-06\",\"section\":\"Not covered by this edition\",\"passage\":\"Not covered by this edition\\nThe standard deduction, the rebate, the health and education cess, surcharge, GST rates and TDS thresholds for tax year 2026-27 were not checked against an official source for this edition, so this bulletin gives no figure for them.\"}]}"}}],"status":{"code":1},"parentSpanId":"fafcf77cf1fc9060"}
